WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:17.883
We were headed west, toward the Indian Ocean, and the Nautilus was traveling quickly.

2
00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:21.224
Where would Captain Nemo's whim carry us next?

3
00:00:21.985 --> 00:00:23.085
Only time would tell.

4
00:00:24.106 --> 00:00:28.628
Every day we were charmed by some new marvel that we saw through the windows of the submarine.

5
00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:34.254
Ned kept trying to vary our diet by introducing some of the foods we had gathered on our

6
00:00:34.374 --> 00:00:35.234
island excursion.

7
00:00:36.315 --> 00:00:41.257
Aside from that, we no longer thought about life on land until something very strange happened.

8
00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:47.439
On January 18, I went up to the platform to greet the day as was my habit.

9
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.322
I waited for the lieutenant to call out his usual phrase, but this time the words were different.

10
00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:58.864
Almost immediately Captain Nemo appeared and scanned the horizon with his telescope.

11
00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:01.033
For some minutes he didn't move.

12
00:01:02.034 --> 00:01:07.858
Then he lowered his telescope and exchanged some words with his lieutenant, who appeared agitated.

13
00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:10.400
The captain, however, remained cool.

14
00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:13.523
What had they seen with their telescopes?

15
00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:16.845
I looked carefully at the horizon but could see nothing.

16
00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.588
The Nautilus was hundreds of miles from the nearest shore.

17
00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:25.532
Pacing the platform, Captain Nemo gave the order for the submarine to speed up.

18
00:01:26.516 --> 00:01:29.678
Just then the lieutenant drew the captain's attention to something.

19
00:01:30.419 --> 00:01:34.622
Captain Nemo stopped pacing and studied the horizon again with his telescope.

20
00:01:35.622 --> 00:01:37.303
I had to find out what they were looking at.

21
00:01:38.044 --> 00:01:41.286
I went to the gallery and retrieved a telescope that I often used.

22
00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:46.589
Back on the platform, I raised it to my eye, but as soon as I did that, the

23
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.231
telescope was snatched away!

24
00:01:49.271 --> 00:01:52.714
I turned around to face Captain Nemo, but I almost didn't recognize him.

25
00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.136
His eyes flashed and his teeth were clenched.

26
00:01:56.852 --> 00:01:58.613
His whole body betrayed his anger.

27
00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:02.594
He did not move while my telescope rolled at his feet.

28
00:02:03.594 --> 00:02:07.095
Had I unwittingly discovered some secret that provoked this fit of anger?

29
00:02:08.515 --> 00:02:12.776
I quickly realized that I was not the object of his hatred because he wasn't looking at me.

30
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.817
His gaze was fixed on some distant point of the horizon.

31
00:02:16.837 --> 00:02:23.959
"Professor Aronnax," he said in a particularly commanding tone, "I now require you to honor your agreement with

32
00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:25.800
me." "What do you mean?"

33
00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:26.752
I asked.

34
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:31.835
"You and your companions must be confined until I decide to release you."

35
00:02:32.896 --> 00:02:35.918
"You're the captain," I said while looking steadily at him.

36
00:02:35.938 --> 00:02:38.559
"But may I ask you one question?"

37
00:02:38.579 --> 00:02:40.200
"You may not."

38
00:02:41.281 --> 00:02:43.482
It would have been useless to try to resist his order.

39
00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:48.965
I went down to the cabin occupied by Ned and Conseil and told them what the captain had

40
00:02:49.005 --> 00:02:53.508
said. You can imagine Ned's reaction, but there was no time for argument.

41
00:02:54.824 --> 00:02:59.185
Four of the crew arrived and conducted us to that cell where we had spent our first night

42
00:02:59.265 --> 00:03:00.186
onboard the Nautilus.

43
00:03:01.266 --> 00:03:04.347
Ned tried to protest, but the door was shut in his face.

44
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:08.108
"Master, will you tell us what this all means?"

45
00:03:08.608 --> 00:03:09.288
asked Conseil.

46
00:03:10.288 --> 00:03:14.949
I had no idea what was going on and could only think of the strange fear on Captain

47
00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:15.690
Nemo's face.

48
00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.970
"Hello! What's this?"

49
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.111
said Ned, interrupting my thoughts.

50
00:03:21.151 --> 00:03:26.045
"Breakfast! But it's only the regular ship's fare, none of my special treats from the island."

51
00:03:26.065 --> 00:03:31.707
"I suggest we eat it," said Conseil, "because we don't know when we'll see our next meal."

52
00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:34.968
We took our seats at the table and ate in silence.

53
00:03:35.729 --> 00:03:39.290
Just then the ceiling light went out, leaving us in total darkness.

54
00:03:40.311 --> 00:03:41.871
"That's all right," said Ned.

55
00:03:41.891 --> 00:03:43.952
"I'm feeling sleepy anyway."

56
00:03:45.293 --> 00:03:48.674
To my astonishment both he and Conseil were soon asleep.

57
00:03:49.454 --> 00:03:53.756
I was wondering why they were so drowsy when I felt myself becoming very tired.

58
00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.823
My eyes closed despite my efforts to keep them open.

59
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:01.146
I began to suspect that our food had been drugged.

60
00:04:02.186 --> 00:04:06.670
Evidently Captain Nemo felt that imprisonment wasn't enough to conceal his actions from us.

61
00:04:07.691 --> 00:04:11.995
I heard the hatches shut and thought I felt the Nautilus descending below the surface.

62
00:04:12.836 --> 00:04:16.078
I fell into a deep sleep filled with nightmares.

63
00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:19.441
The next morning I awoke with a clear head.

64
00:04:20.142 --> 00:04:22.444
To my great surprise, I was in my own room.

65
00:04:23.476 --> 00:04:26.478
My companions undoubtedly had been transferred to their cabin.

66
00:04:27.478 --> 00:04:31.501
I tried my door and it opened, so I was once again free to roam the submarine.

67
00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:35.343
I went up on the platform, where I met Ned and Conseil.

68
00:04:36.304 --> 00:04:39.525
Like me, they had been astonished at waking up in their own beds.

69
00:04:40.526 --> 00:04:43.127
The lieutenant came up and pronounced his usual phrase.

70
00:04:43.828 --> 00:04:45.329
There was no sign of Captain Nemo.

71
00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.632
Later that afternoon I was busy working in the gallery when the captain appeared.

72
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:56.324
I hoped he might give me some explanation for the previous day's events, but he said nothing.

73
00:04:57.205 --> 00:04:58.386
He looked very sad.

74
00:04:59.487 --> 00:05:02.569
After a few minutes he said, "Professor, are you a doctor?"

75
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.951
I was surprised at the question.

76
00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.612
"Yes, I am.

77
00:05:07.053 --> 00:05:09.835
I practiced medicine for several years before I joined the museum."

78
00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:14.139
"Then would you look at one of my men who is ill?"

79
00:05:15.159 --> 00:05:20.364
"Certainly," I said, curious if this man's illness had anything to do with yesterday's mysterious happenings.

80
00:05:21.312 --> 00:05:23.873
Captain Nemo led me to a cabin near the crew's quarters.

81
00:05:24.854 --> 00:05:29.876
On the bed lay a man who was not only seriously ill but also gravely wounded.

82
00:05:30.836 --> 00:05:35.958
His head was covered with a bandage, and when I unwrapped it, I found a devastating injury.

83
00:05:37.019 --> 00:05:38.479
"What caused this wound?"

84
00:05:38.899 --> 00:05:39.340
I asked.

85
00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.541
"Does it really matter?

86
00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:43.001
How is he doing?"

87
00:05:44.022 --> 00:05:48.684
I hesitated to give my opinion, but Nemo reassured me that the man couldn't understand me if I

88
00:05:48.744 --> 00:05:49.364
spoke French.

89
00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.321
"He'll be dead in two hours," I said.

90
00:05:52.341 --> 00:05:54.282
"Nothing can be done to save him."

91
00:05:55.262 --> 00:05:58.484
I was surprised to see tears glistening in Captain Nemo's eyes.

92
00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:01.125
He said, "You may go now, Professor."

93
00:06:02.105 --> 00:06:04.407
For the rest of the day I felt upset.

94
00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:09.989
I slept badly that night and thought I heard distant music that sounded like a funeral hymn.

95
00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:15.952
The next morning Captain Nemo asked if my companions and I could go for another underwater walk.

96
00:06:16.852 --> 00:06:21.356
This time Ned decided to go with us because he regretted having missed our underwater hunt.

97
00:06:22.317 --> 00:06:26.320
Accompanied by Captain Nemo and about a dozen crew members, we left the Nautilus.

98
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:30.903
I recognized at once that we were in the middle of a kingdom made of coral.

99
00:06:32.344 --> 00:06:35.007
Four of the men were carrying an oblong-shaped object.

100
00:06:35.987 --> 00:06:41.692
After walking for about two hours, we came to an area where there was a coral cross surrounded

101
00:06:41.732 --> 00:06:43.353
by small mounds of coral.

102
00:06:44.354 --> 00:06:46.536
Obviously the cross and mounds were man-made.

103
00:06:47.508 --> 00:06:50.269
And then it occurred to me that we were in the middle of a cemetery.

104
00:06:51.229 --> 00:06:55.050
The oblong object was the body of the man who had died the previous night.

105
00:06:56.030 --> 00:07:00.072
A grave was dug and the man was buried with great care and ceremony.

106
00:07:00.812 --> 00:07:03.572
Back onboard the Nautilus, I talked to Captain Nemo.

107
00:07:03.592 --> 00:07:06.553
"That was the man who died last night," I said.

108
00:07:06.573 --> 00:07:11.695
"Yes, now the coral will do its work and cover him for eternity."

109
00:07:12.575 --> 00:07:16.116
Nemo buried his face in his hands and tried to suppress a sob.

110
00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:20.061
"Your dead sleep out of the reach of sharks," I said quietly.

111
00:07:20.081 --> 00:07:24.909
"Yes, sir, of sharks and men," gravely replied the captain.
